<.shell title="Review changes" current={:review_changes}>
  <h1>Review changes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Check the changes to make, then send them.</p>

  <div class="example" onsubmit="return false">
    <.recommended_changes rows={recommendations()} />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every change starts checked. Uncheck one to leave it out.</li>
    <li>
      The checkbox in the header checks or unchecks them all, to send only a few. It shows a
      dash when only some are checked.
    </li>
    <li>A row that can't change says why with a tag, and has no checkbox.</li>
    <li>One button sends the checked changes.</li>
    <li>Below 640px each row stacks, and the header with its checkbox goes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    Give the checkbox column <code>select_all</code>:
    <code>&lt;:col label="" select_all&gt;</code>. Every list with a checkbox on each row and
    one button that sends the checked rows has one.
  </p>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>&lt;.recommended_changes rows=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    from <code>Web.Components.AttendanceImport</code>, as on an activity's Import attendance page, with made-up members.
  </p>
</.shell>
